From b27b7580b4b5119519d5cb60099d22c9388de402 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 19:36:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10457/11362] Record that the in-flight adapter-free eval has
 the tool loop OFF

CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_TOOL_LOOP is not set in the batch runner's environment. I
pinned the GPU, the server binary and the context size and never enabled the
loop, so ten games of live adapter-free induction will produce zero tool-gap
evidence.

That is the miss worth recording: the tool-gap mechanism's stated prerequisite is
live runs WITH the loop on, its adversarial review found the capture path blind
on exactly the path that matters, and the fix has still never been observed
working. It sits at 7 empty rows with its ledger never created -- which cannot
distinguish "the model never wants a tool it lacks" from "we have barely looked".

Also records the open trade for the four remaining batches: enabling selfparse
would buy eight games of tool-gap evidence but changes the configuration, so
those efficiency numbers could not be pooled with batch 1. That is a real choice
about what the remaining GPU hours answer, not a detail to decide silently.

And the prior art that bounds how much the single cd82 result (2 levels, 2459
actions, efficiency 0.0267) should be read into: exp4703/4740 already found
held-out first-win flat, and exp4729 stopped at 20 of 25 games with a resume
note. My run is not the first attempt at this question.

